<title>BELGIUM: Belgium's Quaden sees no delay to EMU start.</title>
<headline>Belgium's Quaden sees no delay to EMU start.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guy Quaden, head of Belgium's new &quot;General Commission on the Euro&quot;, said he expected no delay to the planned January 1, 1999 start of the euro, even if some candidate members were to overshoot deficit targets.</p>
<p>&quot;If the German budget deficit in 1997 were 3.3 percent and the French deficit 3.2 percent -- which is not desirable and at this stage not probable -- can you imagine that state and government leaders would take the historical responsibility to delay the start of the single currency or possibly sink it forever for one or other meagre tenth of a point ?&quot; Quaden said at the Commission's first plenary meeting.</p>
</text>
